    "body": "## Goals\n\nStacked on `modular-editors` (#2469) \u2014 review the diff against that base, not dev. This is the experimental next stage of the same perf program: move semantic computation (statics, elaboration, eval bookkeeping) off the UI thread entirely, so the main thread retains only what keystroke latency needs. Everything here is flag-gated and off by default \u2014 including shadow mode itself, as of the review fixes (it duplicates statics derivation and worker messaging, so it is a development diagnostic: `__w2shadowToggle(true)` enables it, `__w2flip(true)` implies it). The branch exists to de-risk the architecture with parity evidence before any flip.\n\n## What's here\n\n- **Segment-residency protocol**: the worker holds its own copy of the program segment and applies the same edit deltas the main thread does, so semantic requests ship deltas rather than documents. A headless loopback harness parity-gates worker-side state against the main thread's.\n- **Shadow mode**: the app runs the worker pipeline alongside the main-thread one and compares summaries, counting mismatches (`SUMMARY MISMATCH` console reports). This is diagnostic scaffolding, deliberately noisy.\n- **Budgeted synchronous statics**: a small time-budgeted synchronous statics pass for the caret's item only, so type-directed feedback at the caret stays immediate even when full statics moves to the worker.\n- **Worker summary payload + consumer flip**: the view-side consumers can read statics summaries from the worker instead of the main thread, behind a runtime toggle (`__w2flip`).\n- **Instrumentation**: `__staticsProf` per-phase statics-tick diagnostics (gated, zero-cost off); `Test_SerBench` serialization-cost harness (temporary, for the persistence sizing decisions).\n\n## Status / caveats for review\n\n- Codex review findings 1\u20136 are addressed in `d59762623c`: Resident evals are generation-gated (a rejected delta can no longer evaluate the old program under the new generation's label), recovery is immediate and restart-proof (cached authoritative Full resync on NeedResync and on worker restart, before any retried eval posts), flip toggles bust every DefStatics cache (`reset_caches`), summary grafts update the keyed cache entry and schedule a recalculate (durable + observable), and shadow mode defaults off. Gates in `Test_W2Protocol`.\n- Shadow mode (when enabled) reports summary mismatches on some documents; under investigation \u2014 treat the comparison logic itself as review-worthy (false positives are as plausible as real divergence).\n- The residency protocol's delta-application path remains the highest-value review target: it must reproduce main-thread edit semantics exactly (the loopback parity gate covers what it covers, no more).\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n---\n2026-09-09: merged modular-editors forward for the spine elab fix (46bdb6b16e).\n",
